{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:parent-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "The matched frontier recovers the archived downgraded predecessor as a corollary on the identical class: uniformly over \\(n\\geq1\\) and \\(d\\geq2\\), the new upper rate is at most a constant multiple of \\(d/n\\), while its lower rate is at least a constant multiple of \\(\\min\\{1,\\sqrt d/n+d/[n\\log(en)]\\}\\). For every \\(2\\leq d<D_0\\), \\(\\widehat V_{n,d}^{\\mathrm{JF}}=\\widehat V_{n,d}^{\\mathrm{ER}}\\). Separately, along each fixed bounded sequence of alphabets, the risk has two-sided \\(n^{-1}\\) bounds whose comparison constants may depend on \\(\\epsilon\\) and on the sequence and its finite alphabet bound.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(n\\)",
      "\\(d\\)",
      "\\(D_0\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat V_{n,d}^{\\mathrm{JF}}\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat V_{n,d}^{\\mathrm{ER}}\\)",
      "\\(\\epsilon\\)",
      "\\(\\mathfrak R_{n,d,\\epsilon}\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:jackson-factorial-estimator",
      "thm:matched-minimax-frontier",
      "lem:cai-low-absolute-moment-priors",
      "lem:jhw-poisson-l1-lower"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Put\n\\[\n r_{n,d}=\\min\\{1,d/[n\\log(ed)]\\},\n \\qquad a=d/[n\\log(ed)].\n\\]\nSince \\(\\log(ed)\\geq1\\), a two-case check according as \\(d\\geq n\\) or \\(d<n\\) gives \\(r_{n,d}\\leq d/n\\).\n\nNext,\n\\[\n \\frac{\\sqrt d/n}{d/[n\\log(ed)]}=\\frac{\\log(ed)}{\\sqrt d}\n\\]\nis bounded uniformly over integers \\(d\\geq2\\).  If \\(a>1\\), the parent minimum is at most one and hence at most \\(r_{n,d}=1\\).  Suppose \\(a\\leq1\\).  If \\(n\\geq d\\), then \\(\\log(en)\\geq\\log(ed)\\), so\n\\[\n \\frac d{n\\log(en)}\\leq a.\n\\]\nIf \\(n<d\\), put \\(t=d/n>1\\).  The inequality \\(a\\leq1\\) says\n\\[\n t\\leq\\log(ed)=\\log(en)+\\log t.\n\\]\nFor \\(t\\geq2\\), \\(\\log t\\leq t/2\\), hence \\(t\\leq2\\log(en)\\); the case \\(1<t<2\\) obeys the same conclusion after changing the universal constant.  Therefore \\(\\log(ed)\\leq C\\log(en)\\), and \\(d/[n\\log(en)]\\leq Ca\\).  We have proved\n\\[\n \\min\\left\\{1,\\frac{\\sqrt d}{n}+\\frac d{n\\log(en)}\\right\\}\n \\leq C r_{n,d}.                                                     \\tag{23}\n\\]\nApplying \\(\\mathrm{thm:matched\\mbox{-}minimax\\mbox{-}frontier}\\) to these deterministic comparisons proves that the new upper rate is bounded by a constant multiple of \\(d/n\\) and that the new lower rate dominates the stated parent lower expression on the identical model class.\n\nThe equality \\(\\widehat V_{n,d}^{\\mathrm{JF}}=\\widehat V_{n,d}^{\\mathrm{ER}}\\) for \\(2\\leq d<D_0\\) is the first branch of \\(\\mathrm{def:jackson\\mbox{-}factorial\\mbox{-}estimator}\\).  Finally, along a sequence for which \\(2\\leq d\\leq D<\\infty\\), the quantity \\(d/\\log(ed)\\) is bounded above and bounded away from zero.  The matched frontier therefore gives\n\\[\n c_{\\epsilon,D}n^{-1}\\leq\\mathfrak R_{n,d,\\epsilon}\n \\leq C_{\\epsilon,D}n^{-1}\n\\]\nfor all sufficiently large \\(n\\), which is the asserted bounded-alphabet parametric conclusion.  These constants are chosen after fixing the sequence and may depend on \\(\\epsilon\\) and its finite bound \\(D\\).",
    "justification": "This explicit corner check establishes that the run is an estimation refinement of the archived downgraded predecessor rather than a different model or estimand.",
    "gap": "The archived downgraded predecessor leaves a nonmatching bracket and an unresolved consistency region; this proposition records exactly how every certified predecessor conclusion is retained.",
    "consumer": "Downstream users of the predecessor bracket can substitute the matched rate without changing their causal assumptions or scalar target.",
